  "id": "Compound::DB00238 - Gene::1555",
  "verbalization": "Nevirapine and Cyp2b6 exhibit a mechanistically supported relationship through multiple pathways, primarily involving the inhibition of Cyp2b6 by Efavirenz, a non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NNRTI) that is included in the class of non-nucleoside analogs. The evidence suggests that Nevirapine, as part of the non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor class, interacts with Efavirenz, which in turn binds to Cyp2b6. This interaction is consistent across three paths, with the lowest common ancestors indicating a shared classification in the non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor and organonitrogen heterocyclic compound classes. The presence of a direct binding interaction between Efavirenz and Cyp2b6, as well as the inclusion of Nevirapine in the same class as Efavirenz, supports a mechanistic link between the drug and the enzyme. The scores from the paths suggest a strong, biologically plausible relationship, though the exact mechanism of Cyp2b6 inhibition by Efavirenz remains a key area for further investigation.",
